# Deployable defense turrets - the MAST surface.
#
# Placement itself is lm_turret_deploy_tower in turrets.py, so a mission prefab, a comms
# button and the GM console all create turrets the same way and all get the new id back
# synchronously. This file is the author-facing wrapping: discoverable prefabs, and the
# scan text a science officer sees.

=== prefab_lm_turret_tower
" A deployable autonomous defense turret
metadata: ``` yaml
display_text: Defense Turret
type: prefab/turret
side_value: tsn
hull: lm_turret_beam
range: 2500
targets: null
name: Turret #
```
    # `type: prefab/turret` makes this discoverable via labels_get_type("prefab/turret"),
    # so a GM menu can enumerate turret kinds with no hardcoded list: add a hull to
    # shipData_turrets.yaml plus a prefab like this one, and it appears on its own.
    yield result lm_turret_deploy_tower(START_X, START_Y, START_Z, side_value, hull, range, targets, name)


=== prefab_lm_turret_tower_heavy
" A heavy autonomous defense turret - longer reach, harder hitting, slower
metadata: ``` yaml
display_text: Heavy Defense Turret
type: prefab/turret
side_value: tsn
hull: lm_turret_heavy
range: 3500
targets: null
name: Heavy Turret #
```
    # A separate HULL, not a runtime tweak: beam stats live in the engine's ship table and
    # cannot be read or written on a live object, so "a bigger gun" means a new shipData
    # entry. Keep `range` here in step with that entry's beam range.
    yield result lm_turret_deploy_tower(START_X, START_Y, START_Z, side_value, hull, range, targets, name)


=== prefab_lm_turret_tower_drone
" A drone-launching defense tower - the engine flies the drones
metadata: ``` yaml
display_text: Drone Tower
type: prefab/turret
side_value: tsn
hull: starbase_torgoth
range: 1500
targets: null
name: Drone Tower #
behave: behav_npcship
```
    # ENGINE-MEASURED, and it is the whole reason this prefab differs from the others:
    # a hull carrying `drone_launch_timer` DOES make the engine launch drones at a
    # script-set target - but ONLY under behav_npcship. On behav_station it launches
    # nothing, whatever the hull says. (LM_TestRange/maps/test_drone_probe.mast: 5 and 3
    # launches on npcship, 0 on station, against hulls matched but for the timer.)
    #
    # Stock `starbase_torgoth` already carries drone_launch_timer: 30, so a drone tower
    # needs no new shipData and no new art. Deploy pins throttle 0 and target_pos to the
    # spawn point so the npcship helm cannot take it anywhere.
    yield result lm_turret_deploy_tower(START_X, START_Y, START_Z, side_value, hull, range, targets, name, 0, behave)


# Science scan - a turret reads as a fixed emplacement, not a ship and not a station.
//enable/science if has_role(SCIENCE_SELECTED_ID, "turret")
//science if has_role(SCIENCE_SELECTED_ID, "turret")
    + "scan":
        <scan>
            % AUTOMATED EMPLACEMENT: fixed defense turret. No drive, no crew. It engages whatever its owners are at war with.
            % AUTOMATED EMPLACEMENT: defense turret. Immobile and unmanned - it cannot pursue, but it never stops watching.
